WEBVTT

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.240
What?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.700
Monami-chan, you're going to become an idol?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.310
I don't know yet.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.530
For now, I'm just taking lessons.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.250
I see.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.900
You'll probably wear a swimsuit in a gurabia.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.730
Sooner or later they'll take your clothes off.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:19.840
W-What?!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.710
You're the worst!

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.670
What's the matter, Nobu-kun?

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.800
You don't sound like yourself.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.490
Is that so?

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.140
I don't think I'm being any different.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.060
Nobu likes Monami, so he doesn't want her to go and become an idol, right?

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.600
Shut up, stupid Capeta!

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.820
Don't group me with this good-for-nothing!

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.820
When did I say anything—

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.250
G-G-Good-for-nothing?!  What do you mean?!

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.230
If you did your work properly as the manager, I wouldn't have to earn money now, would I?

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.070
A-Are you saying that it's going to be my fault if they take your clothes off?

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.570
That's saying too much, Monami.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.470
No, it's not.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.660
Besides, you can never depend on Nobu when it's really important.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.110
Important, like when?

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.540
You're always like that, aren't you?!

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.550
Calm down, you two.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.880
What's the big deal if she takes her clothes off?

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.800
Shut up!!

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.430
It's because you're always like this that people take you for a fool!

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.340
<i>Capeta and Nobu-kun are working hard to get into the Formula.</i>

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.450
Don't drag me into this!

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.470
<i>And Monami-chan is aiming to become an idol.</i>

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.330
<i>They're all turning into adults.</i>

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.370
Okay, we're here.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.660
Let's hurry.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.620
They're holding the finals for the Formula Stellar first, right?

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.500
It makes your heart race, doesn't it?

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.010
Right, Capeta?

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.760
<i>This is the sound of...</i>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.180
<i>the engine of a real racing machine.</i>

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.120
What are you getting so nervous for?

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.470
We're just here to watch the race today, right?

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.980
It's a preliminary inspection!

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.280
Yeah.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.970
What are you guys doing?

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:13.870
We'll leave you behind!

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.100
Okay!

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.900
<b>Formula Stellar, 5th race, finals.</b>

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:01.670
<b>The curtains will open momentarily here at Shizuoka International Circuit.</b>

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.330
This is amazing.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>The current conditions are:</b>

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.210
Wow!  It's so big!

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.950
<b>humidity 38%, west wind, force 3.</b>

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.100
<b>We're blessed with the best conditions.</b>

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.600
<b>In this race we have a total of 15 entries.</b>

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:19.790
<b>Starting with Sam's Tangent, Belude York,
 Maguyasuto, Drop Technica, Devole—</b>

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:23.370
<b>all teams, battling for the top.</b>

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.980
<b>All cars have now passed the final corner
 and are moving toward the home straight.</b>

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.630
<b>They all finish the formation lap
 and line up on the starting grid.</b>

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.400
<b>Ishihara from Sam's Tangent is in pole position.</b>

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.550
<b>He's won two races and is currently the point leader.</b>

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.140
<b>He is followed by Aizawa from Belude York Motor Sports in second place,</b>

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.450
<b>Sekimoto from Maguyasuto,</b>

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.350
<b>Shimoyama from Drop Technica,</b>

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.350
<b>Sakaguchi from Devole,</b>

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.000
<b>Inoue from D Lock,</b>

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.320
<b>and the 2nd driver from Drop Technica, Takagi.</b>

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.140
Wow.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.320
It sure is impressive when you see it live.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.040
<i>And I'll be riding in one... really soon!</i>

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.610
But I wonder, what came over our boss all of a sudden?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.500
He gave us the 210,000 yen for the audition fees, right?

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:13.450
On top of that, he also told us to go
 for a preview and gave us money for it.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.300
Y-Yeah.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.880
<i>You go fight in my place.</i>

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.480
<i>I'm saying I'll give you the money for the audition.</i>

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:36.280
<i>I'll support you if you're that serious about racing.</i>

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.820
<i>No.  I'll fight along with you.</i>

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.370
<i>Boss.</i>

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.540
<i>However, I can't race.</i>

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:51.540
<i>So, I'll give you the money as though
 I'm racing and fighting, too.</i>

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:56.130
<i>Don't waste this chance once you've accepted the money.</i>

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.970
<i>You understand?</i>

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.060
<i>We'll be one and the same.</i>

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:07.250
<i>You'll have to drive, carrying my spirit on your back.</i>

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.450
<i>And don't you forget that.</i>

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.100
<i>Got it, Capeta?</i>

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.070
<i>Yes.</i>

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.700
<b>All cars have now started!</b>

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.660
<b>A tremendous battle for positions at the first corner...</b>

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:47.430
<b>As expected, Ishihara from Sam's conquers the corner from pole position!</b>

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.330
<b>No!  Aizawa is attacking from the inside!</b>

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>They're neck and neck!  They're neck and neck!</b>

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.850
<b>Ishihara holds his ground!</b>

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.850
<b>Ishihara takes the lead at the first corner!</b>

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.370
<i>W-Wow.</i>

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:04.850
<i>I'm really going to drive that?!</i>

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:07.500
<i>F-For real?!</i>

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.750
Hey, Capeta.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.080
Watch them carefully.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.080
Huh?

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.670
You have to drive in a mock race on the last day of your audition.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.860
You'll be driving the same thing as this, okay?

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.080
What are you getting all pale for?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:23.850
Ow!

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.550
Why are you putting pressure on him like that?!

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.730
You know Ca-chan is timid!

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.670
I didn't mean it like that...

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.420
And you're no better, Ca-chan.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.650
The basics of driving one of these aren't any different from a kart.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.860
It's just loud, has a lid, and is a little faster, right?

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.060
L-Lid?

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.740
Just a little faster...?

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:49.860
<b>Ishihara from Sam's Tangent turns
 the last corner, defending first place.</b>

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.480
<b>Following closely is Aizawa from Belude York.</b>

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.110
<b>And in 3rd place, Sekimoto from Maguyasuto.</b>

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:01.350
<b>In any case, Sam's Ishihara. There is no fault in his driving.</b>

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>It's true that Formula Stellar
 is different from the F1...</i>

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.550
<i>but... it looks so similar.</i>

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:14.400
<i>To be honest, I didn't have any interest back
 then because all I could think of was karting.</i>

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:19.950
<i>But now I want to drive it, this F1-like formula car!</i>

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:20.940
See!

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.140
Just like I said, right?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.680
If you're going to be a racer, aim for the F1!

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.320
If you're aiming for the F1, aim for FSte!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.360
If you pass the audition,
your path to the F1 will instantly open!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.410
Y-Yeah.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.120
I know.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.670
That's why he's...

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.750
Yeah.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.860
Minamoto also got the scholarship last year.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.100
He's one year older than we are,

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:51.470
so when he turns 16 this year and gets permission to enter, he'll probably take part in the races.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.560
But his real battle will be next year.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.360
Next year you'll also...

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.480
I can also enter on the same machine as Minamoto!

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.440
Yeah!

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.730
<b>Final lap!</b>

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.920
<b>The car coming in on the last corner is...</b>

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.400
<b>As expected!  It's still Ishihara from Sam's!</b>

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.870
<b>He's shown a beautiful drive from start to finish.</b>

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.670
<b>Ishihara takes the checkered flag!</b>

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.510
<i>If I work hard, I get to ride one of those.</i>

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.360
<i>If I can ride one of those, I can finally fight him!</i>

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.460
Man!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:34.330
I'm so glad we came to see it!

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:37.440
Next up, it's the F3 and Formula Nippon!

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.650
I'm so happy I could just die!

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.820
Huh?

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.940
Uncle!

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.180
Oh, Monami-chan!

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.240
Taira-kun is with you, I see.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.250
Yeah, he is.

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.420
<i>I see.</i>

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:04.430
<i>Just as I expected.</i>

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.260
<i>Of course he would.</i>

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.000
Is Taira-kun also... taking it{up the butt}?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.930
The Formula Stellar audition?

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:13.630
Yeah, he is.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.150
Then he'll be with our Ryou later.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.800
Which team are you driving with?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.270
Driving with?

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:31.490
Aren't you going to rent an FSte car from one of the teams after the races and practice?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.120
Practice?!

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.540
You can do that?!

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:41.920
W-Well, I heard that those who are taking
 the audition usually practice beforehand, you see.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.240
So we panicked and somehow arranged one through our connections.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:48.550
Taira-kun isn't going to practice?

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:52.500
Hey, Monami!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.410
Hurry up so we can finish our lunch!

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.600
See you later, Uncle.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.460
Bye!

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.980
O-Okay.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.390
Hurry up!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.690
The F3 is gonna start!

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.970
<i>What's Nobu doing?!</i>

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.270
<i>Not knowing something important like this?!</i>

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.950
What?!

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.240
P-Practice?!

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.450
You're kidding me.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.760
So you really didn't know.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.250
Geez.  We really can't depend on you, Nobu.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.050
You say that but... I was...

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.400
It can't be helped.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:30.130
And Nobu really didn't know.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:30.960
You're being soft!

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:35.500
It's because you're too soft on Nobu that things don't work out at the last minute.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.350
It's not Capeta's fault.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:38.770
Hey, hey.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.680
This is no time to be fighting.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.480
That's right...

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:54.370
I was expecting Shiba to come for the FSte audition since he won the last race in Haruna, but...

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.600
I really didn't know!

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:02.170
Everyone borrows a machine and practices for the FSte?!

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:04.580
That's what Oka-chan said.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:10.690
I guess there will be a big gap between those
 who practiced and those driving for the first time, huh?

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:12.950
B-But what should we do?

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:16.250
We have no connections with anyone in the formulas.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.180
Besides, we have no time.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.350
It's next week.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.350
What are we going to do about the audition?

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.120
Damn it!  Whatever!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.660
W-What do you mean, whatever?

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:38.910
You say "practice, practice," but what's so different about the FSte compared with karting?!

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:44.750
Ca-chan is amazing, so he'll be all right without practicing.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.130
B-But unlike in karting, there's gear changes.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.590
What's a gear?!

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:51.900
This?

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.060
FSte isn't automatic?

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.750
So unusual these days.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.510
Of course it isn't, Uncle!

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.100
I've never done gear changes.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.950
Okay then.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.810
Let's practice with this car.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:08.770
Isn't that okay, Uncle?

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.240
Huh?  This car?

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.190
Yeah.  Let's do it, Ca-chan!

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.270
<i>She's right.</i>

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:19.450
<i>I don't have confidence in changing gears on the spot.</i>

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.580
<i>It may be better than nothing to practice with this car.</i>

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:25.540
Yeah.  I'll practice.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.170
Okay.  Let's head back.

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:28.840
We don't need to watch the rest of the races.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.360
Huh?  We're going back now?!

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.580
When the admission fee was 6000 yen?

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:38.800
Where are we going to practice?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:43.880
How about that slope Ca-chan and Nobu drove down a long time ago in the kart?

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:44.890
What?

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:47.660
All of a sudden, when I've never even driven a car before?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:48.810
What are you saying?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.050
You did it on the spot last time too.

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:54.140
B-But I went off the course many times and...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.280
if I go off the course with a real car...

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.550
We can't do that.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:59.620
It's really dangerous there.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.110
Then it's gotta be at the pier.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.830
Can I drive, even though I don't have a license?

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.110
That'll be bad of course.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.900
Then where can we go?!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.120
Wait.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.980
This doesn't seem right.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:14.940
They may both be manual transmissions, but this car is a normal car after all.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.630
It's not the same as a racing machine.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.720
Really?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.480
There'd be a point in practicing if they were the same...

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.270
but they're only similar, so I don't think you should do it.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.060
Don't you see?

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.980
I don't want him getting any bad habits.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:30.810
Nobu...

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:36.260
It's much better risking it on the spot,
rather than getting used to something weird.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.610
Am I wrong?

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:41.160
No, but...

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.120
Believe in yourself!

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.580
Your adaptability is like no other!

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.020
That's right.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:52.590
In your first race, you achieved the course record and won, when it was your first time with an engine.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.560
You'll be okay, Ca-chan.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:00.780
Okay.

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:01.390
I'll try it.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:05.140
There's no point in worrying after all.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.470
That's right!

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.450
You'll definitely be okay, Ca-chan!

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:10.440
Yeah.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.540
Hey, if we weren't gonna practice, we didn't have to head back.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:22.780
We could have watched the F3 and Formula Nippon!

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:31.950
How is it?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.960
The area around my hip is still...

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:34.760
If you'll please.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:35.570
The mat!

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:37.350
Yeah, give me two more.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:45.050
That's great, Noriko.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.890
You're getting better.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:50.560
If you keep this up at the FSte audition, you should be okay.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.470
Souta shortened his time again.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.440
He sure is spirited.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:02.020
He did say he was going to get that FSte scholarship no matter what, after all.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.160
<b>The winner is Isa Hiroshi!</b>

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.160
You did great!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.420
Isa, you're cool!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.790
Look this way!

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.540
We love you, Isa!

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.770
This is Isa Hiroshi.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.070
And this is the rumored Hata Noriko.

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:26.300
Oh.  Hata-san's daughter.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.260
That ex-F3000 driver?

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:29.410
Yeah.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:34.730
She's been given special education since the age of five, and was pretty fast in karts.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:37.700
This year's faces are amazing.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:41.530
We have excellent drivers from all over the country.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:45.380
I wonder who will win out of these.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:49.310
This year looks promising too, don't you think, Tanaka-san?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.630
<i>Taira Capeta...</i>

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:56.890
<i>Do your best.</i>

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:59.550
<i>And whatever you do, don't crash.</i>

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:03.110
Thank you so much for letting me take three days off.

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.510
It may cause a problem though.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.490
What are you talking about?

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:10.030
Capeta-kun is going to take an exam for a university-like place for karts, right?

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.000
No no.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.560
It'll be like a parents' visiting day at school.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.850
You're being modest again.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.690
It's finally the audition, huh.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:24.100
I'd really like to go, but...

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:30.280
I've entrusted my soul to you with the money now.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.240
Y-Yes!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:35.020
Give it all you've got, Capeta.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:38.130
You better pass, no matter what!

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.260
Yes!

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:54.380
Good morning.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.600
Good morning!

00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:01.530
The Formula Stellar Racing School is now in session.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.200
I wonder if Capeta is doing okay.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.130
I wonder what they're doing at the briefing.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.010
I'd like to go in and listen, too.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.080
Then why don't you go?

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.850
They'd probably let you in.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.710
After all, we've paid 210,000 yen.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.450
Y-You think so?

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.270
Then maybe I'll go.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.130
How about you, Monami?

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:27.870
Pass.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.930
You get going.

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.470
And now we will have an introduction from Principal Kagami.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:36.340
Please sit in one of the seats in the back.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.480
Thank you.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:40.460
My name is Kagami.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:43.570
Welcome to the Formula Stellar Racing School.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:51.030
After screening many applicants,
you have all been selected as students.

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:54.080
In the 1st round today, we have 10 people.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:58.580
And over the summer we will hold
 three auditions, making a total of 30 people.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:03.300
Out of these people,
 we will select two or so as scholarship students.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:09.470
It has now been 10 years since this scholarship system has been established...

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:14.750
and Shinkawa, who is here today as an instructor,
 was the first scholarship student.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:20.390
In less than four years, he rose to Japan's top formula and is still playing an active part.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.620
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.810
Putting Shinkawa at the top of the list,

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:25.100
<i>It's Shinkawa from Formula Nippon!  Wow!</i>

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:28.820
our students from the FSRS have left bright records in the world of racing.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:34.910
We hope that all of you will leave remarkable records following in your seniors' footsteps.

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:38.750
But first, there is something we need you to understand.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:45.210
This actually applies to anyone who participates in any motor sport.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:48.570
For example, even in this practice circuit,

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:53.220
a Formula Stellar machine will go up to 170 to 180 kmph.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.160
<i>180 kmph?!</i>

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:59.180
If you have an accident at these speeds, it's a given that you'll be injured.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:01.860
No, you'd be getting off lightly with just injuries.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:06.110
Understand that it's your life on the line here.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:11.570
Moreover, if you damage the car or crash into the guard rails or other equipment...

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:15.530
all damages will have to be compensated.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:21.330
One million, two million... It may even come up to five million yen.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.300
The risk of your life...

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:24.540
The risk of money...

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:30.380
If there's anyone here who's thinking, "I'm not gonna do this unless someone else takes the liability,"

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.800
then we can't have you racing today.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:41.950
Will you all be able to promise me that you will take on these risks yourselves?

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.230
Anyone who can promise me this,
 please raise your hand.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:56.280
Unless you give us your word,
we can't do motor sports with you.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.010
<i>Idiot!</i>

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:59.740
<i>Raise your hand up more confidently, Capeta!</i>

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.670
Yes, all right.  Thank you.

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:09.710
Now that you all have given me your word, we can teach you a lot of things.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:16.830
I hope we can get along nicely for the next three days.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.300
Yes sir!

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.530
The audition's finally started!

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:56.280
I'll get a hold of that scholarship no matter what!

00:22:56.280 --> 00:22:58.730
But I can't get the clutch to connect!

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:00.600
What should I do, Nobu?

00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:02.070
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:03.280
First Step!

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:05.920
Now's the time to break the limit!
